---
import CaseSummary from "@components/CaseSummary.astro";
import Hero from "@components/Hero.astro";
---

<Hero />

<hr />

<section class="text" id="projects">
  <h2>Projects</h2>
</section>

<CaseSummary
  title="Energy Efficiency"
  client="Qatium, 2025"
  tools="Research, ideation, design and front end development."
  tldr="I took a project from 0 to 1 in 4 days. I started with a vague definition of the problem and some raw materials and, collaborating with sales, clients and engineers, came up with a fully formed feature that our clients loved."
  link="/projects/energy-efficiency"
  image="energy-efficiency.png"
/>

<CaseSummary
  title="Qatium.app UI Redesign"
  client="Qatium, 2025"
  tools="Research, Visual & UX Design (Figma)"
  tldr="Qatium.app has evolved organically over the years. Small, focused teams have made improvements in multiple parts of the app, resulting in a design that lacks coherence and polish. Here is a quick attempt at addressing some of the more urgent issues."
  link="/projects/qatium-ui-redesign"
  image="qatium-ui-redesign.png"
/>

<CaseSummary
  title="Improvements to Search feature"
  client="Qatium, 2025"
  tools="Ideation, sketching, coding (TypeScript, CSS), testing (Jest)."
  tldr="I improved the UX for a feature using as little time as possible, going straight to code once a design decision was made."
  link="/projects/qatium-search-improvements"
  image="improvements-to-search-feature.png"
/>

<CaseSummary
  title="Animated round toggle"
  client="Personal project, 2025"
  tools="Figma, React, CSS, Motion.dev"
  tldr="I spent a Friday evening building a round toggle component in React, just to prove myself it could be done."
  link="/projects/roundtoggle"
  image="animated-round-toggle.png"
/>

<CaseSummary
  title="Bankinter, Remastered"
  client="Personal, 2025. Based on a project for Bankinter, 2013"
  tools="Visual Design (Fireworks, Figma), Design Ops"
  tldr="A revision of a project I did for Bankinter in 2013. I took the original design and updated it to 2025 standards, using modern tools and techniques."
  link="/projects/bankinter-remastered"
  image="bankinter-remastered.png"
/>

<hr />

<section class="text">
  <h2>A bit more about me</h2>
  <p>
    I've spent two decades <strong
      >building tools for the people who build things</strong
    >: <a href="https://sketch.com">design tools</a>, <a
      href="https://zenrows.com">development tools</a
    >, <a href="https://qatium.com">engineering tools</a>, <a
      href="https://bebanjo.com">productivity tools</a
    >. I've built things used by millions of people, and things used by just a
    handful — for myself, for my teams, and for the public.
  </p>
  <p>
    I'm comfortable with every step of the product process and can take
    something from 0 to 1, but my true passion is designing things and bringing
    them to life myself. I also love orange, but can use other colors.
  </p>
  <p>
    I'm currently open to senior product design roles — see <a
      href="/how-i-work">how I work</a
    > for more.
  </p>
</section>

